.env
target/
dbt_packages/
logs/
.user.yml
.idea/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# Blanket-ignore .claude/, then re-include the parts that are project code rather than
# local operator state. The blanket pattern is a silent-drop hazard: a new skill, command
# or doc dropped in here is invisible to git and nothing complains (the dispatch
# retro-contract hit exactly this). Directory negations below keep future additions
# visible -- `.claude/*` only matches one level deep, so un-ignoring the directory is
# enough to let everything under it through.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/dispatch.yaml
!.claude/CLAUDE.md
!.claude/commands/
!.claude/skills/
# Deliberately still ignored: settings.local.json (personal overrides), handoff.md
# (ephemeral session state), worktrees/ (agent scratch checkouts).
/tmp/
inbox/
